msgid "Mapping Configuration to Objects"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With config mappings it is possible to group multiple configuration "
"properties in a single interface that\n"
"share the same prefix."
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>@ConfigMapping</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A config mapping requires a public interface with minimal metadata "
"configuration and annotated with the\n"
"`@io.smallrye.config.ConfigMapping` annotation."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `Server` interface is able to map configuration properties with the name "
"`server.host` into the `Server.host()`\n"
"method and `server.port` into `Server.port()` method. The configuration "
"property name to look up is built from the\n"
"prefix, and the method name with `.` (dot) as the separator."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mapping Rules"
msgstr ""

msgid "A config mapping interface must obey the following rules:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A mapping method cannot accept parameters"
msgstr ""

msgid "A mapping method return type cannot be `void`"
msgstr ""

msgid "A mapping cannot use self-reference types"
msgstr ""

msgid "`default` methods are allowed"
msgstr ""

msgid "Registration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a Quarkus application starts, a config mapping can be registered twice. "
"One time for _STATIC INIT_ and a second\n"
"time for _RUNTIME INIT_:"
msgstr ""

msgid "STATIC INIT"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus starts some of its services during static initialization, and "
"`Config` is usually one of the first things that\n"
"is created. In certain situations it may not be possible to correctly "
"initialize a config mapping. For instance, if the\n"
"mapping requires values from a custom `ConfigSource`. For this reason, any "
"config mapping requires the annotation\n"
"`@io.quarkus.runtime.configuration.StaticInitSafe` to mark the mapping as "
"safe to be used at this stage. Learn more\n"
"about xref:config-extending-support.adoc#custom-config-source[registration] "
"of a custom `ConfigSource`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

msgid "RUNTIME INIT"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The _RUNTIME INIT_ stage happens after _STATIC INIT_. There are no "
"restrictions at this stage, and any config mapping\n"
"is added to the `Config` instance as expected."
msgstr ""

msgid "Retrieval"
msgstr ""

msgid "A config mapping interface can be injected into any CDI aware bean:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In non-CDI contexts, use the API `io.smallrye.config."
"SmallRyeConfig#getConfigMapping` to retrieve the config mapping\n"
"instance:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hierarchy"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A config mapping can extend another mapping and inherit all its super "
"members:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Members can also be overridden:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Nested groups"
msgstr ""

msgid "A nested mapping provides a way to subgroup other config properties:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The method name of a mapping group acts as sub-namespace to the "
"configurations properties."
msgstr ""

msgid "Overriding property names"
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>@WithName</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a method name, or a property name do not match with each other, the "
"`@WithName` annotation can override the method\n"
"name mapping and use the name supplied in the annotation:"
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>@WithParentName</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@WithParentName` annotation allows the configuration mapping property "
"to inherit its container name, simplifying the\n"
"configuration property name required to match the mapping:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Without the `@WithParentName` the method `name()` requires the configuration "
"property `server.info.name`. Because we use\n"
"`@WithParentName`, the `info()` mapping will inherit the parent name from "
"`Server` and `name()` maps to `server.name`\n"
"instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "namingStrategy"
msgstr ""

msgid "Method names in camelCase map to kebab-case property names:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The mapping strategy can be adjusted by setting `namingStrategy` value in "
"the `@ConfigMapping` annotation:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@ConfigMapping` annotation support the following naming strategies with "
"the following enum values:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`KEBAB_CASE` (default) - The method name is derived by replacing case "
"changes with a dash to map the configuration property, i.e. `theHost` maps "
"to `the-host`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`VERBATIM` - The method name is used as is to map the configuration "
"property, i.e. `theHost` maps to `theHost`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`SNAKE_CASE` - The method name is derived by replacing case changes with an "
"underscore to map the configuration property, i.e. `theHost` maps to "
"`the_host`."
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>beanStyleGetters</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `beanStyleGetters` attribute (default `false`) enables matching bean-"
"style getter names (`get`/`is` prefixed) to\n"
"their property name equivalent. For example, `getHost()` and `isEnabled()` "
"map to the properties `host` and `enabled`\n"
"respectively:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Conversions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A config mapping class support automatic conversions of all types available "
"for conversion in `Config`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "This is also valid for `Optional` and friends:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this case, the mapping won't fail if there is no configuration property "
"to match the mapping."
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>@WithConverter</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@WithConverter` annotation provides a way to set a `Converter` to use "
"in a specific mapping:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A call to `Converters.foo()` results in the value `bar`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Optionals"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A mapping can wrap any complex type with an `Optional`. `Optional` mappings "
"do not require the configuration path\n"
"and value to be present, so no `NoSuchElementException` is thrown when the "
"configuration property is missing."
msgstr ""

msgid "Collections"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A config mapping is also able to map collections types `List` and `Set`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `List` or `Set` mappings can use xref:config-reference.adoc#indexed-"
"properties[indexed properties] to map\n"
"configuration values in mapping groups. For collection with simple element "
"types like `String`, their configuration\n"
"value is a comma separated string."
msgstr ""

msgid "Maps"
msgstr ""

msgid "A config mapping is also able to map a `Map`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The configuration property needs to specify an additional segment to act as "
"the map key. In this case the `form()` `Map`\n"
"will contain three elements with the keys `index`, `login.page` and `error."
"page`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Do not mix quoted and unquoted forms for the same `Map` key. For a key that "
"spans a single segment, both\n"
"`server.aliases.localhost.name` and `server.aliases.\"localhost\".name` "
"refer to the same key `localhost`, making it\n"
"ambiguous. When SmallRye Config finds both forms it resolves the entry using "
"the quoted form and logs a warning."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When both quoted and unquoted forms are found, only the quoted form is then "
"used to look up values and; property names\n"
"written in the unquoted form are left unmapped and the mapping may fail "
"validation or yield unexpected values. If\n"
"members of a nested group are split between the two forms, the unquoted "
"members are not found and the mapping may fail\n"
"validation or yield unexpected values."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Pick one form and use it consistently for a given key across all "
"configuration sources."
msgstr ""

msgid "It also works for groups:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this case the `allServers()` `Map` will contain one `Server` element with "
"the key `my-server`."
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>@WithUnnamedKey</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@WithUnnamedKey` annotation allows omitting a single map key in the "
"configuration path:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `server.aliases.name` property is unnamed because it does not contain "
"the map key segment. Due to\n"
"`@WithUnnamedKey(\"localhost\")`, the key `localhost` is used automatically "
"when the map key is absent."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the unnamed key is also explicitly set in a property name (e.g. `server."
"aliases.localhost.name=explicit`), the\n"
"explicit value takes precedence over the unnamed entry."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `eager` attribute (default `true`) controls whether the unnamed key "
"entry is included when its values come only\n"
"from defaults. When `eager = false`, the entry is excluded from the `Map` "
"unless at least one value is explicitly\n"
"set in a configuration source."
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>@WithKeys</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@WithKeys` annotation defines which `Map` keys must be loaded by the "
"configuration, instead of discovering keys\n"
"from `Config#getPropertyNames`. This is useful when the `ConfigSource` does "
"not enumerate its properties:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each key must exist in the final configuration relative to the `Map` path "
"segment, or the mapping will fail with a\n"
"`ConfigValidationException`."
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>@WithDefaults</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@WithDefaults` marker annotation on a `Map` returns the default value "
"for the value element on any key lookup:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A lookup with the key `localhost`, `any`, or any other key returns an "
"`Alias` instance populated from `@WithDefault`\n"
"values. A lookup with `prod` returns an `Alias` instance with `name=prod` "
"because the property is defined in the\n"
"configuration. The `Map` can only iterate and size explicitly defined keys — "
"in this case only `prod`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Calling `localhost.name()` returns `localhost`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Calling `any.name()` also returns `localhost`, since it is the default"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Calling `prod.name()` return `prod`, since it is the value defined in the "
"configuration file"
msgstr ""

msgid "Defaults"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@WithDefault` annotation allows to set a default property into a "
"mapping (and prevent and error if the\n"
"configuration value is not available in any `ConfigSource`):"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"No configuration properties required. The `Defaults.foo()` will return the "
"value `foo` and `Defaults.bar()` will return\n"
"the value `bar`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Secrets"
msgstr ""

msgid "A mapping can mark a member as a secret with `Secret<T>`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A `Secret` value modifies the behavior of the Config system by:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Omitting the name of the secret from `Config#getPropertyNames()`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Omitting the name and value of the secret from the mapping `toString` output"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Throwing a `SecurityException` when trying to retrieve the value via the "
"`Config` programmatic API"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A `Secret` can be of any type that can be converted by a registered `org."
"eclipse.microprofile.config.spi.Converter`\n"
"of the same type."
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>toString</code>, <code>equals</code>, <code>hashCode</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the config mapping contains a `toString` method declaration, the config "
"mapping instance will include a proper\n"
"implementation of the `toString` method. The `equals` and `hashCode` methods "
"are included automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "Validation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A config mapping may combine annotations from https://beanvalidation."
"org[Bean Validation] to validate configuration\n"
"values:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The application startup fails with a `io.smallrye.config."
"ConfigValidationException` if the configuration property\n"
"values do not follow the constraints defined in `Server`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mocking"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A mapping interface implementation is not a proxy, so it cannot be mocked "
"directly with `@InjectMock` like other CDI\n"
"beans. One trick is to make it proxyable with a producer method:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `Server` can be injected as a mock into a Quarkus test class with "
"`@InjectMock`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the goal is to only mock certain configuration values and retain the "
"original configuration, the mocking instance\n"
"requires a spy:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `AppConfig` can be injected as a mock into a Quarkus test class with "
"`@Inject`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>ConfigInstanceBuilder</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With the `io.smallrye.config.ConfigInstanceBuilder` API, it is possible to "
"create instances of a config mapping\n"
"interface programmatically, without requiring a `SmallRyeConfig` instance or "
"any configuration source. This is\n"
"particularly useful for testing, providing default configurations, or any "
"scenario where configuration values are\n"
"known ahead of time."
msgstr ""

msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A configuration interface instance is created with `ConfigInstanceBuilder."
"forInterface()`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The builder uses method references to identify which property to set, "
"providing compile-time type safety without\n"
"string-based property names."
msgstr ""

msgid "Primitive Types"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The builder provides dedicated `with()` overloads for `int`, `long`, "
"`double`, and `boolean`. Other primitive types\n"
"(`byte`, `short`, `float`, `char`) use the generic `with()` method with "
"their boxed types:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Optional Properties"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `withOptional()` method sets `Optional` properties. If an optional "
"property is not set, it defaults to empty:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `withOptional` method wraps the value in `Optional.of()`, `OptionalInt."
"of()`, `OptionalLong.of()`, or\n"
"`OptionalDouble.of()` depending on the property type."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Properties annotated with `@WithDefault` are automatically applied when no "
"value is explicitly set in the builder:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Both `host()` and `port()` return their `@WithDefault` values"
msgstr ""

msgid "Explicitly set values override the `@WithDefault` annotation:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Now, `host()` returns `0.0.0.0` and, `port()` returns `8080` from "
"@WithDefault"
msgstr ""

msgid "Nested Groups"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Nested configuration groups are built separately and composed into the "
"parent builder:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Collections and Maps"
msgstr ""

msgid "`List`, `Set`, and `Map` types are set directly with their values:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Required Properties"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Properties without a `@WithDefault` are considered required. Calling "
"`build()` throws a `NoSuchElementException` if\n"
"any required property is not set:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"- Throws a `NoSuchElementException`, the `host` is required but not set"
msgstr ""

msgid "- Works as expected since the `host` value is now provided"
msgstr ""

msgid "Builder Reuse"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A builder instance can be used to produce multiple independent instances. "
"Each `build()` call creates a new object:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`first` and `second` are equal but not the same object"
msgstr ""
